                    <div class="explainer-text">
                        <h3>1. video decoding</h3>
                        <p>The browser's built‑in <span class="highlight">Media Source Extensions</span> and <span class="highlight">HTML5 video</span> API handle the heavy lifting.</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Demuxing:</strong> The container (MP4, WebM) is split into separate video and audio streams.</li>
                            <li><strong>Decoding:</strong> The compressed video frames (H.264, VP9, etc.) are decoded into raw YUV or RGB pixel data.</li>
                            <li><strong>Frame access:</strong> We use <code>video.currentTime</code> and draw the current frame onto a hidden canvas using <code>ctx.drawImage(video)</code>.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p style="color:#666666; font-size:0.8rem; margin-top:0.3rem;">This happens entirely in the GPU, making it extremely fast and power‑efficient.</p>
