                    <div class="explainer-text">
                        <h3>2. frame grabbing &amp; scaling</h3>
                        <p>Each frame is extracted and preprocessed in a few simple steps:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Grabbing:</strong> <code>drawImage()</code> copies the current video frame onto a small offscreen canvas.</li>
                            <li><strong>Scaling:</strong> The canvas dimensions are set to <span class="highlight">chars/line × scale</span> (width) and the height is computed automatically to preserve aspect ratio, using a correction factor for monospace characters (<code>0.52</code>).</li>
                            <li><strong>Resolution control:</strong> Lower scale (0.25× – 0.5×) reduces detail but speeds up processing, while higher scale (2× – 4×) captures fine details for large‑format ASCII art.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p style="color:#666666; font-size:0.8rem; margin-top:0.3rem;">The scaling is done using <span class="highlight">bicubic interpolation</span> (the browser's default) for smooth results.</p>
                    </div>
