                        <h3>5. rendering &amp; export</h3>
                        <p>The final ASCII grid is displayed in the output area and can be exported in multiple formats:</p>
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Live preview:</strong> The text is rendered in a monospace font, with your chosen font family and size.</li>
                            <li><strong>PNG (raster):</strong> Each ASCII frame is drawn onto a canvas with a monospace font and saved as a PNG image.</li>
                            <li><strong>SVG (vector):</strong> The ASCII text is wrapped in an SVG <code>&lt;text&gt;</code> element, producing a scalable, resolution‑independent graphic.</li>
                            <li><strong>TXT (plain):</strong> The raw ASCII string is saved as a plain text file.</li>
                            <li><strong>Video (MP4):</strong> The tool plays the video at normal speed and captures each frame using a canvas stream. The canvas dimensions are adaptively scaled to fit your ASCII grid while keeping the pixel count within a safe limit (4M pixels). The encoding uses a reasonable bitrate to keep file sizes manageable.</li>
